    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19354" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gedrōsi</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cedrōsi</span></b> , ōrum,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γεδρωσοὶ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γαδρωσοί</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γαδρώσιοι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of Asia</i>, in the modern <i>Mekran</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 8, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 20,
				23, § 78</span></i>; called also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gedrōsii</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cedr-</span></b> ), <i><span class="en">Curt. 9,
				10, 3</span></i>; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gedrūsi</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Plin. 6,
				23, 25, § 94 sq.</span></i>— <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gedrōsĭa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cedr-</span></b> ), ae,
				f., <i>the country of the Gedrosi</i>:
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γεδρωσία</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κεδρωσία</span>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 21,
				11, 36, § 62</span></i>.</div>
